    "number": 247,
    "title": "docs: expand setup instructions for Windows contributors",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds comprehensive Windows (PowerShell) setup instructions and ensures all tooling works cross-platform.\n\nCloses #205\n\n## Changes\n\n- **CONTRIBUTING.md**: Restructured setup section with dedicated Linux/macOS and Windows subsections. Added step-by-step PowerShell commands for toolchain installation, Dylint setup, clone/build, and quality checks. Added Windows tip about shell compatibility.\n- **README.md**: Added a Windows-specific note about installing Dylint via PowerShell after setting up Rust through rustup.\n- **CI matrix**: Updated .github/workflows/lint.yml and \templates/github-action.yml to run on both ubuntu-latest and windows-latest with a \fail-fast: false strategy matrix.\n- **docs/integration.md**: Updated the GitHub Actions section to document the dual-OS matrix.\n- **.github/scripts/validate-toolchain-pins.ps1**: New PowerShell drift-guard script that mirrors the existing bash version — validates nightly toolchain pins and clippy_utils rev consistency on Windows.\n\n## Testing\n\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check passes\n- cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings passes\n- cargo test --workspace passes\n- PowerShell drift-guard script validates successfully on Windows\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Code follows existing project conventions (edition 2024, let-chains, existing lint pass structure)\n- [x] All CI checks pass (Linux + Windows matrix)\n- [x] Documentation updated for Windows contributors\n- [x] Drift guard script available for both bash and PowerShell",
